esources 5 but it could just translate to extra merits and bonus points like them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Salary is likely gone as well. Iron Siaka in Adversaries is an Essence 3 Bronze Faction Sidereal and she has Resources 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T11:58:25-07:00","id":1308752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1308750#post1308750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Salary is likely gone as well. Iron Siaka in Adversaries is an Essence 3 Bronze Faction Sidereal and she has Resources 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see if that's a placeholder. Because salary IS a key facet of sidereal background due to how yu-shan is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-29-2019, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:00:21-07:00","id":1308753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1308752#post1308752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll see if that's shorthand or not. Because salary IS a key facet of sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Was. We have no idea how they currently work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T12:20:38-07:00","id":1308756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1308743#post1308743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they explicity didn't which is why basic salary was pretty much resources 5 but it could just translate to extra merits and bonus points like them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1308752#post1308752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll see if that's a placeholder. Because salary IS a key facet of sidereal background due to how yu-shan is.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the first, I feel as though Salary doesn't necessarily equate to Sidereals being afforded greater resources, but is a matter of the exchange rate.<br /> <br /> That is to say, you can exchange a coin of ambrosia for a coin of jade by spending a mote. In Heaven, that will buy you a song, because Heaven is awash with luxury. In Creation, that will buy you a small house. I don't think either has much to do with how they're trained.<br /> <br /> Salary is no less important for Sidereals than Resources is for Dynasts, and yet you still start with 0 and have to dedicate dots to actually play somebody living at the minimum expected lifestyle of a Prince of the Earth. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T09:51:30-07:00","id":1313509,"title":"","content":"I'm slightly wary of their ability to fight battle groups in their own games.<br /> <br /> Due to the focus on martial arts your typical Sidereal circle has a predisposition to have a number of unarmoured or lightly armoured characters and excellencies with (+essence) defence won't be much help there while the PCs are low essence. Like we're not talking about a circle of Sidereals making a stand against an army so much as encountering a bunch of hungry ghosts while investigating a new Shadowland.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T10:18:28-07:00","id":1313516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313509#post1313509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm slightly wary of their ability to fight battle groups in their own games.<br /> <br /> Due to the focus on martial arts your typical Sidereal circle has a predisposition to have a number of unarmoured or lightly armoured characters and excellencies with (+essence) defence won't be much help there while the PCs are low essence. Like we're not talking about a circle of Sidereals making a stand against an army so much as encountering a bunch of hungry ghosts while investigating a new Shadowland.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't really know until we see the charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T10:42:15-07:00","id":1313517,"title":"","content":"The previews in Adversaries of the Righteous were pretty accurate for Dragon-Blooded and Lunars at least as far something as basic as dice caps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T11:54:58-07:00","id":1313533,"title":"","content":"They\u2019ll presumably still have their TN manipulator charms too. If they can use that offensively and give people trying to hit them TN 8 or 9 and/or remove double 10s, that should give them a significant enough defense bonus to handle anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T12:55:48-07:00","id":1313547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313533#post1313533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They\u2019ll presumably still have their TN manipulator charms too. If they can use that offensively and give people trying to hit them TN 8 or 9 and/or remove double 10s, that should give them a significant enough defense bonus to handle anything.</div> </div> </div> </div> My problem isn't that there won't be a charm to fix it, it's the idea of needing charms for something so basic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T13:30:47-07:00","id":1313549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313547#post1313547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My problem isn't that there won't be a charm to fix it, it's the idea of needing charms for something so basic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to dodge by giving someone TN 8 or 9 is a much better defense than just a static defense. That's basically removing 10% of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T13:45:12-07:00","id":1313552,"title":"","content":"I'm probably in the minority, but I really would like 3rd ed Sids to focus more on the Astrology and Loom of Fate stuff rather than the martial arts. SMA gets held up in 1st and 2nd ed as being the Sids ~thing~, and I think that misses the point of what they're supposed to be. They're Exalted by the Maidens of Destiny, not the Maidens of Supernatural Ass Kicking.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of flavor stuff I want to see - less monolithic Gold vs. Bronze faction stuff for one. Starting characters actually feeling important in the setting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Maybe Silver Faction being an actual thing?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25290-palmedfire","name":"palmedfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25290_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-21T14:38:45-07:00","id":1313560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>palmedfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313552#post1313552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SMA gets held up in 1st and 2nd ed as being the Sids ~thing~, and I think that misses the point of what they're supposed to be. They're Exalted by the Maidens of Destiny, not the Maidens of Supernatural Ass Kicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>The person who created the point of what Sidereals were supposed to be developed both the idea that mastery over destiny would extend to superlative martial arts prowess (especially in a setting of the game's genre) and liked the idea of the educated manipulators pulling double duty as ultimate killing machines in contravention of typical genre fiction.<br /> <br /> Also, are the Maidens of Battles and Endings not Maidens of Supernatural Ass Kicking?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T10:31:22-07:00","id":1313697,"title":"","content":"Thinking on this a bit, I feel like using Essence as a dice cap is a bad idea, especially for a group of Exalted that have a large number of Elders running around. Every other dice cap is something you can start with at chargen and then branch out and the game tends to be careful with cap breaking effects, so most elders aren\u2019t rocking effects that grant them an insurmountable dice advantage.<br /> <br /> However, with Sidereals, a 1 die dice cap on your dice adder is terrible so there\u2019s a natural desire to want to make it better. But, with Chejop and Anys Syn running around, anything you do to improve a starting character\u2019s dice cap needs to not accidentally grant them an insane dice pool either. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it\u2019s probably better to just have the TN manipulator charms be the Sidereals \u201cExcellency\u201d and add in other dice adder charms that specify their own limits or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T10:35:32-07:00","id":1313699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313560#post1313560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The person who created the point of what Sidereals were supposed to be developed both the idea that mastery over destiny would extend to superlative martial arts prowess (especially in a setting of the game's genre) and liked the idea of the educated manipulators pulling double duty as ultimate killing machines in contravention of typical genre fiction.<br /> <br /> Also, are the Maidens of Battles and Endings not Maidens of Supernatural Ass Kicking?</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re also there to fulfill the \u201cWise Old Martial Arts Mentor\u201d trope. Back in the 1e core, they pretty much said that\u2019s exactly what the Gold faction was: five-ish ancient Sids who fucked off to the end of the world and hid, but would be willing to teach the returning Solars their ancient kung fu secrets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T11:16:15-07:00","id":1313709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313697#post1313697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think it\u2019s probably better to just have the TN manipulator charms be the Sidereals \u201cExcellency\u201d and add in other dice adder charms that specify their own limits or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> Going by <i>Adversaries of the Righteous</i>, TN manipulation is an innate quality of their Excellencies alongside the bonus dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T12:27:21-07:00","id":1313722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313560#post1313560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The person who created the point of what Sidereals were supposed to be developed both the idea that mastery over destiny would extend to superlative martial arts prowess (especially in a setting of the game's genre) and liked the idea of the educated manipulators pulling double duty as ultimate killing machines in contravention of typical genre fiction.<br /> <br /> Also, are the Maidens of Battles and Endings not Maidens of Supernatural Ass Kicking?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think Grabowski was resistant to the idea of groups of Exalted who were explicitly not meant to have combat oriented characters within them (all that stuff about &quot;You're in a kung fu movie! You don't get to just gesticulate magically! Fight!&quot;). As is right and proper! SMA is really a way to unique way to enable that for &quot;elder characters&quot; and a play on the Sidereals established synergy between fate and the martial arts (called out clearly in our first introduction to them in the 1e Core, as you note).<br /> <br /> And yes, it is fun to subvert the trope (although seen from wuxia / chanbara traditions, is that so much a subversion or a &quot;played straight&quot;?).<br /> <br /> Still I have sympathy with palmedfire's point that I don't want too much focus on the SMA, but I trust developers to get the balance right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313699#post1313699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in the 1e core, they pretty much said that\u2019s exactly what the Gold faction was: five-ish ancient Sids who fucked off to the end of the world and hid, but would be willing to teach the returning Solars their ancient kung fu secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that? I can't remember anything in the 1e core about teaching Solars ancient special martial arts or anything. <br /> <br /> Now my bias is openly against SMA as being of much importance as something for Sidereals to teach Solars (in order to fulfill a role as mentors and teachers), but I'm absolutely sure there wasn't anything like that in there. <br /> <br /> 1e core Gold Faction were pretty cool in a distinct way from their later incarnation (a bunch of &quot;hermits and savants&quot; distributed through the world who were *really* focused on the Cult of the Illuminated in a way that was de-emphasized in later material), but I don't think them Sidereals having limited numbers and there being few Gold Faction, nor Sidereals having special secret martial arts came into the picture then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:40:35-07:00","id":1313833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313697#post1313697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on this a bit, I feel like using Essence as a dice cap is a bad idea, especially for a group of Exalted that have a large number of Elders running around. Every other dice cap is something you can start with at chargen and then branch out and the game tends to be careful with cap breaking effects, so most elders aren\u2019t rocking effects that grant them an insurmountable dice advantage.<br /> <br /> However, with Sidereals, a 1 die dice cap on your dice adder is terrible so there\u2019s a natural desire to want to make it better. But, with Chejop and Anys Syn running around, anything you do to improve a starting character\u2019s dice cap needs to not accidentally grant them an insane dice pool either.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think it\u2019s probably better to just have the TN manipulator charms be the Sidereals \u201cExcellency\u201d and add in other dice adder charms that specify their own limits or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some things to potentially learn from Dragon-Blooded here.<br /> <br /> It would make thematic sense for the default Sidereal PC being an essence 2 character and reserve essence 1 for the very newly Exalted. Also how Dragon-Blooded Excellencies work could help to address the disparity between abilities you primarily roll vs. those you use to calculate a static value.<br /> <br /> Elders are less of a concern for me, you could easily say the excellency caps at 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T11:43:38-07:00","id":1313874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313833#post1313833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's some things to potentially learn from Dragon-Blooded here.<br /> <br /> It would make thematic sense for the default Sidereal PC being an essence 2 character and reserve essence 1 for the very newly Exalted. Also how Dragon-Blooded Excellencies work could help to address the disparity between abilities you primarily roll vs. those you use to calculate a static value.<br /> <br /> Elders are less of a concern for me, you could easily say the excellency caps at 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it makes thematic sense for Sids to start at essence 2, but I think the main reason DBs get it by default is so that you can do mixed games without totally overshadowing DBs right out of the gate. As such, I suspect Sids will start at essence 1 like the other Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> As for elders, I agree that their playability and strength is not really something I care about, beyond preventing another round of \u201cChejop jumps out of your teacup and uses Creation-Slaying Oblivion Kick to kill your great great grandparents and prevent you from ever existing\u201d memes from being created. That said, I\u2019ll admit that my initial thought was that their dice cap could be (essence or 3, whichever was better) which would just feel weird with a cap of 5 on top of that. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think threading the needle of \u201cnot making starting players sadface,\u201d \u201cpreventing elders from getting too many dice,\u201d and \u201cnot giving the Sids so many dice that their TN manipulators turn into I Win buttons\u201d is difficult but doable. And probably does lie in starting players getting fairly crap for a dice cap, so they have to use their dice tricks more often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T11:51:22-07:00","id":1313877,"title":"","content":"I think that if the default assumption for Lunars is that you're playing somebody who has been Exalted for about a year, the same will hold with Sidereals.<br /> <br /> There might be some underlying reasons for Dragon Blooded to start at 2, but going by what the developers seemed to say the most the primary reason seems to be that playing a Dragon Blood who has only been Exalted for a year means playing a child, and outside of a specific niche that's a bit of a no-go.<br /> <br /> I feel as though presuming a Sidereal who has been Exalted for the time it takes to reach Essence 2 as the default leaves some awkward hanging questions about what kinds of grand adventures that they had in that time (that also never end up occurring in play).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T12:36:24-07:00","id":1313884,"title":"","content":"Assuming Sidereal excellency is as their QCs currently have it (+[Essence] dice &amp; TN=4 for 8m 1wp), an elder has about 75% chance to get 2-3 more successes than a fresh Solar, but the fresh Solar can get better odds than the elder if she gets double 8s or better through Charms.<br /> <br /> Given this, I'm guessing Sidereals won't get double 8s and 7s (or only very rarely), so they will be better on a typical roll but become outmatched once Charms get going.<br /> <br /> it's also worth noting that Sidereals need to pay wp to lower their target numbers, so they likely won't be able to use their full Excellency as often as other Celestials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-23-2019, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T16:39:24-07:00","id":1313934,"title":"","content":"I just assume Sidereals will end up having dice-adder or success-adder excellencies and Target Number manipulation will come in the form of Charms. If you think about it, &quot;Broadly manipulate fate for it to conspire in your favor&quot; is better represented by success-adding than by Target Number manipulation, which sounds like modifying specific actions to make them insanely easier to succeed at. It would help a lot with some of the balance concerns around Sidereal excellencies, particularly how massively powerful Sidereals with Light Artifact Weapons become compared to other weapons, and how non-Charm adders and dice tricks become unfeasible in any significant amount, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T23:14:24-07:00","id":1313996,"title":"","content":"The dice cap is likely not as big a concern as folks think in part due to the fact that the Excellency might have TN-manipulation built into it. Also remember that dice aren't an IC-thing, and so &quot;I need more Excellency&quot; is less a reason someone like Chejob might pursue higher Essence (I'm actually skeptical that he's the sort to be that) and more because they well, want to for weird sidegrade powers like we saw in Lunars.<br /> <br /> I'd be surprised if many Sideereal elders are even higher than Essence 6 when it comes about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T12:05:05-07:00","id":1317219,"title":"","content":"I'd like Sidereals to have the Mastery tag, absolutely. I think a <i>Sidereal </i>tag would open up some good mechanics for handling the Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to have a <i>Blatancy </i>merit. For two dots, a Sid can stand up in front of a crowd, announce that she's going to use magic to sway their opinion, and then proceed to do so. Much like a modern hypnotist act. For four dots, she can spy on her enemies by standing behind a cardboard cutout of a bush.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T12:07:55-07:00","id":1317221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1313996#post1313996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be surprised if many Sideereal elders are even higher than Essence 6 when it comes about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, considering that a handful of the greatest and most powerful Lunars who remember the First Age are Essence 6, and likely none are Essence 7, I imagine that's pretty much the same for the Sidereals.<br /> If they decide that Chejop should have the highest Essence of any Exalt in the game, it'll probably be 7, not the 9 he had in 2e. But I think there's a good chance even he will only have Essence 6.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T13:44:19-07:00","id":1317230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317221#post1317221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, considering that a handful of the greatest and most powerful Lunars who remember the First Age are Essence 6, and likely none are Essence 7, I imagine that's pretty much the same for the Sidereals.<br /> If they decide that Chejop should have the highest Essence of any Exalt in the game, it'll probably be 7, not the 9 he had in 2e. But I think there's a good chance even he will only have Essence 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksi is Essence 7 as of the Lunars Kickstarter preview. In practice this just means she has larger mote pools than Lilith or Ma-Ha-Suchi as they each only get one unique &quot;Elder Prowess&quot; charm, but they don't seem to be making Essence 6 the absolute cutoff. I'd expect to see Chejop at 7 based on that, but if they want to make him the highest Essence Exalt rather than equal highest he'd need to be at least 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12165-speedbump","name":"Speedbump","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-08T18:57:31-07:00","id":1317266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Speedbump</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317230#post1317230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raksi is Essence 7 as of the Lunars Kickstarter preview. In practice this just means she has larger mote pools than Lilith or Ma-Ha-Suchi as they each only get one unique &quot;Elder Prowess&quot; charm, but they don't seem to be making Essence 6 the absolute cutoff. I'd expect to see Chejop at 7 based on that, but if they want to make him the highest Essence Exalt rather than equal highest he'd need to be at least 8.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's likely not the highest Essence Exalt; Rakan Thulio seems like a better candidate, considering he is at least the oldest Exalt alive. I'd say Chejop and people like Anys Syn would hit 7, like Raksi. And Rakan about 8, tops, if he's given the highest Essence. Otherwise a 7 as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T09:43:56-07:00","id":1317366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317266#post1317266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He's likely not the highest Essence Exalt; Rakan Thulio seems like a better candidate, considering he is at least the oldest Exalt alive. I'd say Chejop and people like Anys Syn would hit 7, like Raksi. And Rakan about 8, tops, if he's given the highest Essence. Otherwise a 7 as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering he's much older than raksi he should be at least at 8. Even in the first edition i remember it being implied that he was at 8 or 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-09T13:35:40-07:00","id":1317400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317366#post1317366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering he's much older than raksi he should be at least at 8. Even in the first edition i remember it being implied that he was at 8 or 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence doesn't have a lot of this &quot;You're this old, you get this Essence&quot; this edition. It's much more about personal development at 6+ and how much the indivdiual thinks that becoming more attune to their Essence will better how they want to do things. Chejob seems much more to me as a workaholic more interest in managing material and temporal issues, rather than high minded esoterica that I think greater Essence is implied to work with.<br /> <br /> He had Essence 10 in previous editions in part beucase Essence was assumed to just be maxed-out for the assumed age of a particular character whenever possible, rather than having anything to do with actual interest in such things by the indivdiual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T06:01:04-07:00","id":1317784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317400#post1317400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essence doesn't have a lot of this &quot;You're this old, you get this Essence&quot; this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually been the reality of the situation in any edition. First and second edition are full of NPCs who haven't achieved the optimal essence for their age, it's just that it tended to be used to reafirm that NPC write-ups sucked.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T07:18:17-07:00","id":1317794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317400#post1317400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essence doesn't have a lot of this &amp;quot;You're this old, you get this Essence&amp;quot; this edition. It's much more about personal development at 6+ and how much the indivdiual thinks that becoming more attune to their Essence will better how they want to do things. Chejob seems much more to me as a workaholic more interest in managing material and temporal issues, rather than high minded esoterica that I think greater Essence is implied to work with.<br /> <br /> He had Essence 10 in previous editions in part beucase Essence was assumed to just be maxed-out for the assumed age of a particular character whenever possible, rather than having anything to do with actual interest in such things by the indivdiual.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to check, but I'm pretty sure that in 2nd ed he had Essence 9. Which surprised people, but IIRC the point was that he was too busy, and too invested in his own ideology to achieve true perfect enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T07:19:40-07:00","id":1317795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317366#post1317366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering he's much older than raksi he should be at least at 8. Even in the first edition i remember it being implied that he was at 8 or 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is he still much older than her? Not saying he isn't, but I am wondering if either of their ages are mentioned anywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T09:44:29-07:00","id":1317828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317784#post1317784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not actually been the reality of the situation in any edition. First and second edition are full of NPCs who haven't achieved the optimal essence for their age, it's just that it tended to be used to reafirm that NPC write-ups sucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly remember for a lot of 1e and 2e a lot of what felt liek infalted Essence stants. You had a lot of 5s about for anyone who was decently old, and then you had basically everyone over 100 as Essence 6, many Essence 7s and 8s about. 2e in particular I remember having a lot of 8-10 NPCs around, including Chejob specifically as a result of what I sitll was a view that 5,000 years old = <i>has</i> to be Essence 10.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T10:33:47-07:00","id":1317832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317795#post1317795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is he still much older than her? Not saying he isn't, but I am wondering if either of their ages are mentioned anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's still 5000 according to his chapter fiction. I don't think we've got an age on TQoF this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T14:23:45-07:00","id":1317875,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, 5000 doesn't mean he was born shortly after the Primordial War anymore, since they seem to have moved from the Primordial War ending 5000 years ago to the First Age being 5000 years long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-11T18:47:17-07:00","id":1317933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317366#post1317366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering he's much older than raksi he should be at least at 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are probably a few Lunars who are noticeably older than Raksi that are Essence 4.<br /> <br /> Chejop is probably quite puissant among the Exalted, but that's not going to be because of his age, but because he's a significnt architect of the Usurpation, the major guiding hand of the Realm through the Immaculate Order, and just has a general demeanour of &quot;I have to take responsibility for ensuring the continued future of everything&quot;, as we see in his core book chapter fiction.<br /> <br /> You can probably be Essence 6 when you're about 150 if you manage to achieve a legend of grandeur and distinction even by the standards of the Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T04:10:02-07:00","id":1318011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317933#post1317933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are probably a few Lunars who are noticeably older than Raksi that are Essence 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked Vance a while ago about the Essence scores of surviving First Age elders once, as I was wondering if Essence 5 was a pretty reasonable score for a First Age Lunar (the ones in the book have Essence 6+, but they're particularly famous ones), and he said not all First Age Lunars are even Essence 5. And if Raksi's still one of the youngest First Age Elders, that does indeed mean there's Lunars older than her who are Essence 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 06-12-2019, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T04:40:00-07:00","id":1318015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317933#post1317933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can probably be Essence 6 when you're about 150 if you manage to achieve a legend of grandeur and distinction even by the standards of the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm.....<br /> <br /> I think I wouldn't want this to be a thing that really happens much in the setting; I really like the chart in the corebook that suggests most Exalts of a few hundred years are still Essence 3. (It's important because of how there's literally thousands of Dragonblood who are a few hundred years old.)<br /> <br /> But theoretically possible yes, because I'm sure some ST somewhere is going to have a game where the players reach 1000xp when they've been exalted for like 10 years, and is going to think about maybe giving them Essence 6.<br /> <br /> I mean, in the game I play, the PCs already have nearly 500xp, solidly into Essence 5, and they've been exalted for 1-30 years. Obviously I don't want them to go up to 6 (they can just fill out into different areas), but if we're still playing this game in 5 years, then I don't see a reason the game should tell the ST that they can't be Essence 6, if that's he wants to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T05:32:30-07:00","id":1318027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318015#post1318015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I wouldn't want this to be a thing that really happens much in the setting</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do I. Grandeur and distinction by the standards of all Exalted shouldn't come cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-12T13:27:53-07:00","id":1318103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317366#post1317366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering he's much older than raksi he should be at least at 8. Even in the first edition i remember it being implied that he was at 8 or 9.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being older than her does not mean he has a higher Essence. He could have <i>lesser</i> Essence, even. Age matters when determining Essence, but not to the extent that you cannot see a Shogunate Elder outstripping a First Age or even Divine Revolution Elder at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T20:23:36-07:00","id":1318384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1317875#post1317875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, 5000 doesn't mean he was born shortly after the Primordial War anymore, since they seem to have moved from the Primordial War ending 5000 years ago to the First Age being 5000 years long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the lore changed raksi was born around the near end of the first age where as kejak was born near the beginning. Now, he's probably near the middle but he probably still had time to raise his essence before usurpation. Moreover, most of his work is probably delegated unless sidereals manage to acquire the best multitasking charms in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:01:42-07:00","id":1318394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318384#post1318384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the lore changed raksi was born around the near end of the first age where as kejak was born near the beginning. Now, he's probably near the middle but he probably still had time to raise his essence before usurpation. Moreover, most of his work is probably delegated unless sidereals manage to acquire the best multitasking charms in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Raksi being born shortly before the Usurpation was only from 2e. It's not said much on her in the 3e write-up besides her being a philsopher and scholar anda ll that before it, so she may or may not be.<br /> <br /> A big thing on Essence this edition seems to be whether the person like, cares enough to do it or not. Raksi does. Chejob while having a lot of delegated tasks, is always depicted as a selfless workaholic, not the sort to have minions do all the tedious stuff so he can sit on a mountain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:04:01-07:00","id":1318396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318394#post1318394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Raksi being born shortly before the Usurpation was only from 2e. It's not said much on her in the 3e write-up besides her being a philsopher and scholar anda ll that before it, so she may or may not be.<br /> <br /> A big thing on Essence this edition seems to be whether the person like, cares enough to do it or not. Raksi does. Chejob while having a lot of delegated tasks, is always depicted as a selfless workaholic, not the sort to have minions do all the tedious stuff so he can sit on a mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps but I do find it hard to believe that the preeminent sidereal has low essence for an elder his age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:10:42-07:00","id":1318397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318396#post1318396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps but I do find it hard to believe that the preeminent sidereal has low essence for an elder his age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't since Essence rating isn't an IC thing and as stated a few times, it's not something that in itself gives you political power. There's no &quot;Need Essence this refined to play&quot; card about and a lot of his power comes from political weight, more than his magicalness IMHO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:14:34-07:00","id":1318398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318397#post1318397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't since Essence rating isn't an IC thing and as stated a few times, it's not something that in itself gives you political power. There's no &quot;Need Essence this refined to play&quot; card about and a lot of his power comes from political weight, more than his magicalness IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree because both of them are pretty important. Especially when it comes to Yu-shan where Essence and magicalness is part of surviving in yu-shan especially it's politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:20:31-07:00","id":1318400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318398#post1318398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree because both of them are pretty important. Especially when it comes to Yu-shan where Essence and magicalness is part of surviving in yu-shan especially it's politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Higher Essence does nothing for his ability to be a good politican and administrator. Stats don't get any higher, and his ability to have connections with people isn't either. Essence being thsi dick-measuring stat that is super important to gods probably matters less this edition than you know, what actual political clout the god has and personal ability to do shit. I think the entire idea that you're judged by how many dots in magic stat you have is probably irrelevant in general since well, it's no more relevant in heavenly politics in my mind than it would be my ability to weight press says somethinga bout my ability to participate in DC politics.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-13T21:29:54-07:00","id":1318403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318400#post1318400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Higher Essence does nothing for his ability to be a good politican and administrator. Stats don't get any higher, and his ability to have connections with people isn't either. Essence being thsi dick-measuring stat that is super important to gods probably matters less this edition than you know, what actual political clout the god has and personal ability to do shit. I think the entire idea that you're judged by how many dots in magic stat you have is probably irrelevant in general since well, it's no more relevant in heavenly politics in my mind than it would be my ability to weight press says somethinga bout my ability to participate in DC politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point has more to his ability to be able to defend himself especially versus people who do want to kill him. His original background not only put him as one of the best politicians in creation but also one of the best fighters and his ability to defend himself against assassins would be a necessary trait to have in the vicious circle of yu-shan politics.<br /> <br /> Also I'll just cut to where it explicitly says it in 1e. Page 80 of sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....Gods prostate themselves before him, and he has long since mastered all the martial arts of his order. His greatest skill is his mastery of astrology, allowing him to read the future in the flows of Essence from the Loom of Fate. He uses this knowledge to choose his course of action, never wavering once it is set. </div> </div> </div>It also talks about how good his lore and sorcery are but I feel like this was probably the most important part. The book also calls him the wisest and most powerful sidereal and possibly the most powerful living exalt and not just because his political grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-14-2019, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T01:18:34-07:00","id":1318428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318403#post1318403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point has more to his ability to be able to defend himself</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's your point, then your point is blatantly wrong. This is third edition; Essence 6+ isn't a new tier of power.<br /> <br /> For example, just on on May 29th the Devs said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1315170#post1315170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6+ is all plateau. We don't want players to feel that they need shenanigans to hit Essence 6 or 7+ in order to play in the big leagues.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1295469-ask-the-devs-v2?p=1315252#post1315252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't make them mechanically more powerful than Essence 5 Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T10:38:03-07:00","id":1318499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318428#post1318428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's your point, then your point is blatantly wrong. This is third edition; Essence 6+ isn't a new tier of power.<br /> <br /> For example, just on on May 29th the Devs said:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine but that doesn't really change what I said. Not having them more mechanically powerful than E5 doesn't mean that a man of kejak's capabilities should be at low essence given his original write up. Kejak was a man who not only spent his life working towards his goals but also trained his body and his mind and his mystical powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T10:42:53-07:00","id":1318500,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's fair. If being Essence 8 doesn't give Chejop loads of power, that doesn't mean he's not essence 8... in fact, it maybe means him being essence 8 is less problematic for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T10:48:44-07:00","id":1318501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318500#post1318500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's fair. If being Essence 8 doesn't give Chejop loads of power, that doesn't mean he's not essence 8... in fact, it maybe means him being essence 8 is less problematic for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'll be interesting to see how SMA works now, especially considering that Chejop's original write up said he basically mastered them all. Now, it'll obviously be weaker than it used to be but the real question is if some SMA will still have high essence values and the what the implications of those higher essence values are as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T10:55:17-07:00","id":1318503,"title":"","content":"Didn't the devs said that Sidereal Martial Arts would start on Essence 4? If so, I figure they'd be Essence 4 and 5, since they don't want to have any Charms that require Essence 6 or higher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T11:00:24-07:00","id":1318504,"title":"","content":"I didn't read much of Exalted except the splats of 3e, but the core book puts a lot of emphasis on Sideral Martial Arts as being very core to their concepts. If you can't use it before essence 4 (so something like 35 seances I believe) it'd be a mistake I believe, except if they have a special connection so SMA which let them learn it from low essence or something I guess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T11:04:05-07:00","id":1318505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318504#post1318504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read much of Exalted except the splats of 3e, but the core book puts a lot of emphasis on Sideral Martial Arts as being very core to their concepts. If you can't use it before essence 4 (so something like 35 seances I believe) it'd be a mistake I believe, except if they have a special connection so SMA which let them learn it from low essence or something I guess</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll be waiting a few years before finding out how they work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-14T15:55:25-07:00","id":1318559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318403#post1318403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point has more to his ability to be able to defend himself especially versus people who do want to kill him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essence 3-5 can do that.<br /> <br /> I expect Chejop to be higher, but again, that's representative of the scope of the legend depicted in his corebook fiction, not a bar he has to cross in order to do something basic.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T03:35:39-07:00","id":1318639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318504#post1318504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't read much of Exalted except the splats of 3e, but the core book puts a lot of emphasis on Sideral Martial Arts as being very core to their concepts. If you can't use it before essence 4 (so something like 35 seances I believe) it'd be a mistake I believe, except if they have a special connection so SMA which let them learn it from low essence or something I guess</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, normal Martial Arts generally go from Essence 1-3, so it makes sense to me that first you learn a normal Martial Art, and then this enables you to get to the point where you're enlightened enough to grasp the extremely esoteric Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> I can't really imagine a young guy, freshly Exalted, using Sidereal Martial Arts. Surely it's for wizened old masters with long white bears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T03:41:16-07:00","id":1318642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318639#post1318639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, normal Martial Arts generally go from Essence 1-3, so it makes sense to me that first you learn a normal Martial Art, and then this enables you to get to the point where you're enlightened enough to grasp the extremely esoteric Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> I can't really imagine a young guy, freshly Exalted, using Sidereal Martial Arts. Surely it's for wizened old masters with long white bears.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true but it does make it unfeasible foe moat games with sucks. E3 would be a little more useful for sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T03:47:26-07:00","id":1318643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1318639#post1318639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, normal Martial Arts generally go from Essence 1-3, so it makes sense to me that first you learn a normal Martial Art, and then this enables you to get to the point where you're enlightened enough to grasp the extremely esoteric Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> I can't really imagine a young guy, freshly Exalted, using Sidereal Martial Arts. Surely it's for wizened old masters with long white bears.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess time will prove one of us wrong because I don't think I'd appreciate the design of what seems a really fun feature unique to one of the splat behind an Essence gate that high (I'd be good if it was about Essence 2 or any RolePlay limitations &quot;You must first reach the summit of this Glass Tower while blind to unlock your 15th Chakra&quot;), but I'd much appreciate that Sidereals are in nature able to commune with these mystical shenanigans martial arts that no mere mortal can fathom.<br /> <br /> I mean maybe I overthought the importance these SMA had for Sidereals while reading the Core Exalted 3e and I went all very hyped making false assumptions in my head, that could be that as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-15T05:07:50-07:00","id":1318652,"title":"","content":"I guess I can see where you're coming from. I suppose that, as I've played/run like 60 sessions of Essence 4-5 Exalted, and run 4 sessions of Essence 1, I have quite a different viewpoint from you guys.<br /> <br /> I think Essence 1 or 2 would be way too low for the pinnacle of Sidereal power, but I could see Essence 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T16:46:49-07:00","id":1318971,"title":"","content":"The core book description of Solar Exalted describes part of their essential experience as being mastery of sorcery, and yet Solar Circle still eludes them until Essence 5.<br /> <br /> I find the core book description of the Sidereal Exalted to phrase their relationship with the martial arts in about the same manner. That doesn't mean that Sidereal Styles have to wait until Essence 5, but I do think they need to wait for a while.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, you've got plenty of other very impressive martial arts to manage. As they currently are, they already have qualities based on differing levels of presumed mastery; if Sidereals have a means of using Styles with the benefit of the Mastery keyword, that's already a leg up over the vast majority of Creation's martial artists.<br /> <br /> And as we've seen with Dragon Blooded and Lunars, the fully written up Exalted are informed by the guidelines laid down by the core, but are not beholden to them. Not to mention how the Sidereals book will almost definitely include writers who did not work on the core, some of whom will be assigned mechanics. There's every possibility that between now and then, somebody will pitch an idea for a neat and distinctive additional permutation or elaboration of what Sidereals can do in &quot;regular&quot; Martial Arts with their sutras or something, and it will enrich the image of them as hidden sage masters of the fist.<br /> <br /> I like... the premise and some of the associated imagery of Sidereal Martial Arts, but I feel as though making them available too early risks overshadowing the other Styles, with which I think Sidereals should also have a strong relationship.<br /> <br /> I also think Sidereal Martial Arts need a careful overhaul in which they still feel distinctly powerful with a mandate other than being a substitute for Exalted Charms of Essence 6+, which was its whole other bag of worms.<br /> <br /> Because the other side is that I feel as though Sidereal Martial Arts that are available from Essence 1 while still having that kind of power... it might mess up some setting and balance considerations. I mean, unless they had Essence 1 Charms that didn't do anything too heavy, but that feels as though it belies the point of Sidereal Martial Arts in general, and why people want earlier access to them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Still, I can't help but consider the comparison with Artifacts of different levels; you still get to do some distinctly powerful things from the outset with your Stormcallers and Forgotten Blades, and considerations such as Artifacts having distinct rules and premises from Martial Arts, or the necessary efforts in play or character creation to be granted such an Artifact, do not quite feel sufficient. There might not be a flawless answer.<br /> <br /> But it informs my thinking that Sidereal Martial Arts not being available from the outset is not outrageous.<br /> <br /> As regards Chejop, I don't think that a premise of mastering all or most of the Sidereal Arts is essential to his character. Honestly, it always read a bit perfunctorily to me, informed not so much by him being particularly devoted to the martial arts as the fact that there was literally no other way to represent him being an elder Sidereal. It's just &quot;hey, Chejop Kejak has been Essence 8 for the last 800 years, so he might as well learn all of the Sidereal Martial Arts, because otherwise about half of those dots are going to waste and he's barely distinguishable from a regular Sidereal&quot;. It would have made them look bad compared to the presumed space of Lunars of similar Essence.<br /> <br /> Here we have an Edition in which an Exalt of Essence 6+ being indistinguishable in all but the lightest ways from one at Essence 5 is by design, Sidereals are still going to have a closed Charm set but it's promised to be bigger and a bit more diverse, and Sidereal Martial Arts are not pulling double duty as elder Sidereal Charms. I think those considerations warrant reviewing whether or not Chejop needs to be deeply associated with the Sidereal Martial Arts. I don't expect Chejop to be devoid of martial arts, but maybe they're not a deep focus for him anymore, and he could get an Elder Charm based more on prophetic insight and offering firm guidance to authorities such as the Scarlet Empress and the Mouth of Peace.<br /> <br /> Really, in a system where there isn't a presumption that all elder Sidereals need such Arts to have anything worth a damn once they rise above Essence 5, I think it would be valuable to have an elder Sidereal who specifically does not have Sidereal Arts, to convey the statement that they aren't the be-all end-all to upper levels of Sidereal power.<br /> <br /> (A lot of which means that the basic character of Chejop Kejak would probably still function if he was, like, Essence 4)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-16T17:03:40-07:00","id":1318978,"title":"","content":"I kind of assumed SMA are going to be a bit like Signature Charms for DBs. Something you wont's ee in chargen, but something you can grow into after a game's been going for a bit. Them going Essence 3-5 is aboutw here I expect them since it helps fill in for MAs in general and it allows the Charms toh ave good &quot;Breathing room&quot; in power too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T08:36:56-07:00","id":1319288,"title":"","content":"My expectations about SMA is mainly because of my personnel experience : I know for a fact with the groups of people I play with that I will never see any of them is they are beyond Essence 4, and it's only a small chance if they are Essence 3.<br /> <br /> Which of course incline me to hope they will be available from quite early like other MA","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T09:14:44-07:00","id":1319302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1319288#post1319288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of course incline me to hope they will be available from quite early like other MA</div> </div> </div> </div>Whereas I'd hope they wouldn't completely eclipse actual Sidereal Charms or other martial arts. It's hard to imagine a Sidereal player even <i>considering</i> Crane Style (a martial arts style which, I'll remind y'all, was introduced in a Sidereal supplement) when something like Obsidian Shards of Infinity is accessible at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T09:21:49-07:00","id":1319304,"title":"","content":"While I'd be happy for SMA to be, say, Essence 3, I think actually an Essence 1 Obsidian Shards (which would obviously be much weaker, as it's Essence 1) might not be a good first choice over Crane, because it's likely expensive, difficult to use, and lacking in bread-and-butter effects (which Sidereals have generally had problems with anyway, a deliberate weakness of their design).<br /> <br /> Though of course, since they'll presumably get 15 charms, and you can only take 2 or 3 Crane charms at Essence 1 anyway, it's quite probable that a character whose concept is all about being a Martial Artist will take 2 different styles anyway, so they've got more than a 5th of their charms as Martial Arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-18T09:57:26-07:00","id":1319311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1319302#post1319302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas I'd hope they wouldn't completely eclipse actual Sidereal Charms or other martial arts. It's hard to imagine a Sidereal player even <i>considering</i> Crane Style (a martial arts style which, I'll remind y'all, was introduced in a Sidereal supplement) when something like Obsidian Shards of Infinity is accessible at character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with that considering I can cover MA with most other splats and had the opportunity to see 2-3 MA in my campaigns already. Furthermore I don't expect SMA to be better than other MA, but I hope they cover narratives and aesthetics regular MA do not cover.<br /> <br /> I don't believe I'm going to convince anyone on this subject, I'm just sharing my hopes for accessible SMA from a requirement standpoint.<br /> <br /> Considering Sorcery and Solars, even Essence 1 Solar shines already in sorcery. Between the reduce cost of Sorcery and the sheer power of the solars, Workings of Ambition 1 Solar are in their range, and maybe even Solar 2 if everyone in the team decides to go for it. But as I stated it doesn't matter, it has more to do with my own expectations than a logical argumentation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T16:30:59-08:00","id":1497862,"title":"","content":"So\u2026 Sidereals is on kickstarter. Thoughts, hopes, ideas for the new direction of this most manipulative of splats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T16:31:38-08:00","id":1497863,"title":"","content":"Triple post, sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-22T16:33:22-08:00","id":1497864,"title":"","content":"Triple post, sorry!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T02:14:56-08:00","id":1500912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1497862#post1497862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So\u2026 Sidereals is on kickstarter. Thoughts, hopes, ideas for the new direction of this most manipulative of splats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Necessarily post-hoc, but...<br /> <br /> I think they did a very good job of repackaging the familiar old classic powers to the new Edition, and particularly gave Abilities that had been new to Second a new lease on life. I like many of the new Charms as providing tools for Sidereals to fulfil their purposes in very human ways (I particularly like that one Serenity Charm to comfort a person as they sleep and cause them to have greater confidence in speaking freely when they wake), and Maiden Charms are a nice way to round them out and distribute their power to bless and curse.<br /> <br /> I think Prophecies are a good successor to Astrology, capturing a lot of the core concept while both streamlining it and repackaging it in terms of their conduct as seers, while still having just enough interaction with the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> <br /> I find Sidereal Martial Arts to have done a good job of threading the needle of becoming more accessible, mechanically coherent, and within reason while still managing to be crazy powerful. Obsidian Shards of Infinity should cause incredulity in anybody who needs to fight it, but doesn't have to create its own ad hoc mechanical standards to do its thing. Also I quite like how Violet Bier of Sorrows gets to be its own fighting style with distinct characteristics rather than just a bunch of workmanlike combat enhancers.<br /> <br /> The Bureaus of the Celestial Bureaucracy got presented in a very vivid and lively way that allows one to effectively set a scene of working within them and what kinds of stories might come out of their agendas and activities, and Yu-Shan feels like a very living and breathing place in a way that very much facilitates telling a variety of stories taking place entirely there. The main thing I like about Heaven is how focusing its activities on crafting and fulfilling destinies gives a firm sense of and stakes to what it actually does, and the emphasis on divine purviews as bestowed by the Bureaucracy helpfully clarifies the extent of what gods are and do.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-27T22:27:49-08:00","id":1501518,"title":"","content":"So, I love a number of things I read in the kickstarter document. I love the description of how the Bureau of Destiny handles the actual duties is great. Like I don't recall if this was in 2e or not, but I remember Sids being the errand boys sent out for every little thing and all the messes, as opposed to the new one where Sids feel more like they're thrown into a situation because its too important to allow to go wrong and/or there is literally no other way to make it work.<br /> <br /> I also like that there's descriptions of the different divisions and how they work. Heck I just appreciate that we have an idea on how the Bronze and Gold factions work as more long term groups since 2e I don't recall any description of how the factions worked beyond them being based on how they stood on the Usurpation which was always baffling to me. It just struck as like saying your government's major parties were defined by who you're siding with in the Peloponnesian wars.<br /> <br /> Also I laughed at the mention that the Bureau of endings is also the home of experts in extremely random or specific things because they've all collectively decided they need hobbies to deal with work.<br /> <br /> This has been a recurring thing, but I adore the major factions (dynast aside) not forcing membership. That they offer it and try to sell it is fine, but that the Sids are willing to go, &quot;Okay look we are the ones best able to relate to the things that have happened, and help you with what you're going through. That said if you don't want the job its always open if you want to talk.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 01-29-2023, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T03:10:47-08:00","id":1501682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1501518#post1501518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I don't recall if this was in 2e or not, but I remember Sids being the errand boys sent out for every little thing and all the messes, as opposed to the new one where Sids feel more like they're thrown into a situation because its too important to allow to go wrong and/or there is literally no other way to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think it's a presentation of specialised duties that mean in a game focused on Sidereals it would make sense that they'd have a lot of time to hang around Yu-Shan and get involved with its municipal disputes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T03:56:29-08:00","id":1501796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1501518#post1501518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I love a number of things I read in the kickstarter document. I love the description of how the Bureau of Destiny handles the actual duties is great. Like I don't recall if this was in 2e or not, but I remember Sids being the errand boys sent out for every little thing and all the messes, as opposed to the new one where Sids feel more like they're thrown into a situation because its too important to allow to go wrong and/or there is literally no other way to make it work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the fanbase had a fixation with them as <i>the most overworked people ever</i> that kinda ate into the scope of them being player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T21:08:42-08:00","id":1503728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1308398-3rd-ed-sidereals?p=1501796#post1501796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the fanbase had a fixation with them as <i>the most overworked people ever</i> that kinda ate into the scope of them being player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>3E Sidereals give me strong Spectre vibes, whic